tion/"}, {"title": "Anthropic, ACN To Invest $1B Each In Frontier AI Evaluation Over Five Years", "url": "https://stocktwits.com/news-articles/markets/equity/anthropic-acn-to-invest-1-billion-each-in-frontier-ai-evaluation-over-five-years/cZtH7kMRBEX"}, {"title": "Anthropic, ACN To Invest $1B Each In Frontier AI Evaluation Over Five Years", "url": "https://stocktwits.com/news-articles/markets/equity/anthropic-acn-to-invest-1-billion-each-in-frontier-ai-evaluation-over-five-years/cZtH7kMRBEX?.tsrc=rss"}, {"title": "Best AI model by november 2026 ↗", "url": "https://cryptobriefing.com/anthropic-grants-metr-access-to-ai-models-for-safety-and-transparency-push/"}, {"title": "Anthropic, Accenture Announce $2 Billion AI Model Evaluation Plan", "url": "https://www.gktoday.in/anthropic-accenture-announce-2-billion-ai-model-evaluation-plan/"}, {"title": "anthropic metr independent evaluators", "url": "https://ai-tldr.dev/releases/anthropic-metr-independent-evaluators/"}]}, "The search turned up coverage of Anthropic's October 15, 2026 announcement about METR, and it's consistent across the sources I found.\n\n- **The announcement:** One outlet reports that Anthropic began giving employee-like access to an embedded team from METR, a nonprofit that evaluates frontier AI models. Six METR employees have been onboarded with company hardware, office space, and access to internal tools and systems.\n- **Access level:** Anthropic says the team's access is roughly on par with what its own risk assessment teams have. A second source says the team is siloed from other METR staff and works under enforceable agreements.\n- **Publication rights:** One summary says METR can publish its analysis; Anthropic can only require redactions in narrow, predefined categories. This is a secondary summary, so check Anthropic's own post for the exact terms.\n- **Evaluator criteria:** Anthropic's stated requirements include expertise, independence, sufficient access, and freedom to publish observations and assessments of a model or a process.\n- **Background:** Anthropic and Accenture announced a partnership on September 18, 2026, with each company committed at least 1 billion over five years. Faculty, Accenture's AI business, will lead the work. The source also says Anthropic is exploring pilots with nonprofit evaluator METR and others.\n\nThe sources are mostly secondary coverage (Unite.AI, AI/TLDR, Crypto Briefing), and I didn't find Anthropic's original post in these results. The Crypto Briefing item also carried an unrelated prediction-market header."], "durationSeconds": 6.627833499999999, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01EzP7hgTSp557nFxPRK8wYW", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
